// How wide a thing is on screen, from its size out here.
function skyPixels(earthRadii, radius) { return earthRadii * radius; }

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ orbits
//
// The rings are the picture. At true scale a planet is a floored dot and the
// only thing on the stage carrying any information about where it is are the
// circles it goes round on: the spacing of the orbits is what says inner system
// and outer system, and the gap between Mars and Jupiter is what says there is
// a belt in it. Without them the solar system is nine dots in the dark and
// could be anything.
//
