// order and the unit walks there over as many turns as it takes.
//
// `move_to` cannot express that: `path_to` seeds its search with the unit's
// remaining movement, so anything further comes back "unreachable". The
// engine's long-range router — the one the AI has always used — does express
// it, and `/route` hands back the next step of it. So a travel order is a
// standing order the client re-issues each turn: ask for the step, move onto
// it, stop when there is no step left.
